<concept id="datasketches_functions">

  <title>Impala DataSketches Functions</title>

  <titlealts audience="PDF">

    <navtitle>DataSketches Functions</navtitle>

  </titlealts>

  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <data name="Category" value="Impala"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Impala Functions"/>
      <data name="Category" value="SQL"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Aggregate Functions"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Data Analysts"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Developers"/>
      <data name="Category" value="Querying"/>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>

  <conbody>

    <p>
      <indexterm audience="hidden">DataSketches functions</indexterm> The DataSketches
      functions estimate distinct counts and quantiles from sketches, which are compact
      summaries of the data. For example, you can store one sketch for each day in a
      table and merge the sketches later to estimate the distinct values of a month. The
      functions use the
      <xref href="https://datasketches.apache.org/" scope="external" format="html">Apache
      DataSketches</xref> library.
    </p>

    <p>
      A sketch is a <codeph>BINARY</codeph> value. The functions return and accept
      sketches as <codeph>BINARY</codeph>, and you store them in <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
      columns. See <xref href="impala_binary.xml#binary"/>.
    </p>

    <p>
      The following table lists the supported sketch types.
    </p>

    <table id="ds_sketch_types">
      <tgroup cols="3">
        <colspec colname="1" colwidth="1*"/>
        <colspec colname="2" colwidth="1*"/>
        <colspec colname="3" colwidth="4*"/>
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry>Sketch type</entry>
            <entry>Function prefix</entry>
            <entry>Purpose</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>HLL</entry>
            <entry><codeph>ds_hll_</codeph></entry>
            <entry>Distinct count.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>CPC</entry>
            <entry><codeph>ds_cpc_</codeph></entry>
            <entry>Distinct count. Smaller than an HLL sketch of the same
              accuracy.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>Theta</entry>
            <entry><codeph>ds_theta_</codeph></entry>
            <entry>Distinct count with set operations: union, intersection, and
              difference.</entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>KLL</entry>
            <entry><codeph>ds_kll_</codeph></entry>
            <entry>Quantiles, ranks, and distribution of <codeph>FLOAT</codeph>
              values.</entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </tgroup>
    </table>

    <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/usage_notes_blurb"/>

    <p rev="5.0.0 IMPALA-9821">
      Before <keyword keyref="impala50"/>, sketches were <codeph>STRING</codeph> values.
      A query that passes a <codeph>STRING</codeph> sketch fails with a
      <codeph>No matching function</codeph> error. To migrate, see
      <xref href="impala_incompatible_changes.xml#incompatible_changes_500x"/>.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can read the <codeph>BINARY</codeph> sketches that Hive writes and merge them
      with the sketches that Impala creates. The exception is HLL and CPC sketches of
      <codeph>STRING</codeph> values. Impala and Hive hash these strings differently, so
      a merged sketch counts the same string twice. For a compatible sketch, use
      <codeph>CAST(<varname>col</varname> AS BINARY)</codeph> in Hive.
    </p>

    <p conref="../shared/impala_common.xml#common/example_blurb"/>

<codeblock>-- Store one HLL sketch of the visitors for each day.
CREATE TABLE visitor_sketches (visit_date DATE, visitors BINARY)
  STORED AS PARQUET;
INSERT INTO visitor_sketches
  SELECT visit_date, ds_hll_sketch(user_id) FROM visits GROUP BY visit_date;

-- Estimate the distinct visitors for each day.
SELECT visit_date, ds_hll_estimate(visitors) FROM visitor_sketches;

-- Merge the sketches to estimate the distinct visitors for all days.
SELECT ds_hll_estimate(ds_hll_union(visitors)) FROM visitor_sketches;

-- Estimate the median of a column.
SELECT ds_kll_quantile(ds_kll_sketch(CAST(price AS FLOAT)), 0.5) FROM sales;
</codeblock>

    <section id="ds_aggregate_functions">

      <title>Aggregate Functions</title>

      <p>
        The aggregate functions create a sketch or an estimate from the values of a
        group, or merge the sketches of a group. They ignore <codeph>NULL</codeph>
        values, and the HLL, CPC, and Theta functions also ignore empty strings. Unless
        stated otherwise, a function returns <codeph>NULL</codeph> for a group without
        other values.
      </p>

      <p>
        Impala supports the following DataSketches aggregate functions:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_cpc_sketch">DS_CPC_SKETCH</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_cpc_sketch_and_estimate"
            >DS_CPC_SKETCH_AND_ESTIMATE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_cpc_union">DS_CPC_UNION</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_sketch">DS_HLL_SKETCH</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_sketch_and_estimate"
            >DS_HLL_SKETCH_AND_ESTIMATE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_union">DS_HLL_UNION</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_sketch">DS_KLL_SKETCH</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_union">DS_KLL_UNION</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_intersect"
            >DS_THETA_INTERSECT</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_sketch">DS_THETA_SKETCH</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_sketch_and_estimate"
            >DS_THETA_SKETCH_AND_ESTIMATE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_union">DS_THETA_UNION</xref>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <dl>
        <dlentry id="ds_cpc_sketch">

          <dt>
            DS_CPC_SKETCH(type a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Creates a CPC sketch of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>.
            <p id="ds_sketch_argument_types">
              <b>Argument type:</b> <codeph>TINYINT</codeph>, <codeph>INT</codeph>,
              <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>, <codeph>FLOAT</codeph>, <codeph>DOUBLE</codeph>, or
              <codeph>STRING</codeph>. You must cast other types, for example
              <codeph>SMALLINT</codeph>, <codeph>DECIMAL</codeph>, or
              <codeph>DATE</codeph>, to one of these types.
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_cpc_sketch_and_estimate">

          <dt>
            DS_CPC_SKETCH_AND_ESTIMATE(type a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>, computed with a CPC sketch.
            <p conref="#datasketches_functions/ds_sketch_argument_types"/>

            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_cpc_union">

          <dt>
            DS_CPC_UNION(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges the CPC sketches of the group into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_sketch">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_SKETCH(type a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Creates an HLL sketch of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>.
            <p conref="#datasketches_functions/ds_sketch_argument_types"/>

            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_sketch_and_estimate">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_SKETCH_AND_ESTIMATE(type a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>, computed with an HLL sketch.
            <p conref="#datasketches_functions/ds_sketch_argument_types"/>

            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_union">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_UNION(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges the HLL sketches of the group into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_sketch">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_SKETCH(FLOAT a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Creates a KLL sketch of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> The function also accepts integer types. You must cast
              <codeph>DOUBLE</codeph> values to <codeph>FLOAT</codeph>.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_union">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_UNION(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges the KLL sketches of the group into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_intersect">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_INTERSECT(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns a Theta sketch of the values that are in every sketch
            of the group.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_sketch">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_SKETCH(type a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Creates a Theta sketch of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>.
            <p conref="#datasketches_functions/ds_sketch_argument_types"/>

            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Returns an empty sketch, not <codeph>NULL</codeph>, for
              a group without values.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_sketch_and_estimate">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_SKETCH_AND_ESTIMATE(type a)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of the values of
            <codeph><varname>a</varname></codeph>, computed with a Theta sketch.
            <p conref="#datasketches_functions/ds_sketch_argument_types"/>

            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Returns 0, not <codeph>NULL</codeph>, for a group
              without values.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_union">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_UNION(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges the Theta sketches of the group into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

      </dl>

    </section>

    <section id="ds_scalar_functions">

      <title>Scalar Functions</title>

      <p>
        The scalar functions read and combine sketches. Unless stated otherwise, a
        function that takes one sketch returns <codeph>NULL</codeph> for a
        <codeph>NULL</codeph> sketch. The query fails if a value is not a sketch of the
        expected type.
      </p>

      <p>
        Impala supports the following DataSketches scalar functions:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_cpc_estimate">DS_CPC_ESTIMATE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_cpc_stringify">DS_CPC_STRINGIFY</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_cpc_union_f">DS_CPC_UNION_F</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_estimate">DS_HLL_ESTIMATE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_estimate_bounds_as_string"
            >DS_HLL_ESTIMATE_BOUNDS_AS_STRING</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_stringify">DS_HLL_STRINGIFY</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_hll_union_f">DS_HLL_UNION_F</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_cdf_as_string"
            >DS_KLL_CDF_AS_STRING</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_n">DS_KLL_N</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_pmf_as_string"
            >DS_KLL_PMF_AS_STRING</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_quantile">DS_KLL_QUANTILE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_quantiles_as_string"
            >DS_KLL_QUANTILES_AS_STRING</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_rank">DS_KLL_RANK</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_kll_stringify">DS_KLL_STRINGIFY</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_estimate">DS_THETA_ESTIMATE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_exclude">DS_THETA_EXCLUDE</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_intersect_f"
            >DS_THETA_INTERSECT_F</xref>
        </li>

        <li>
          <xref href="#datasketches_functions/ds_theta_union_f">DS_THETA_UNION_F</xref>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <dl>
        <dlentry id="ds_cpc_estimate">

          <dt>
            DS_CPC_ESTIMATE(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of a CPC sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_cpc_stringify">

          <dt>
            DS_CPC_STRINGIFY(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns a readable summary of a CPC sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_cpc_union_f">

          <dt>
            DS_CPC_UNION_F(BINARY sketch1, BINARY sketch2)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges two CPC sketches into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Ignores a <codeph>NULL</codeph> argument. Returns an
              empty sketch if both arguments are <codeph>NULL</codeph>.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_estimate">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_ESTIMATE(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of an HLL sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_estimate_bounds_as_string">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_ESTIMATE_BOUNDS_AS_STRING(BINARY sketch [, INT kappa])
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of an HLL sketch with its
            lower and upper bounds, as a comma-separated string.
            <codeph><varname>kappa</varname></codeph> is the number of standard deviations
            of the bounds: <codeph>1</codeph>, <codeph>2</codeph> (default), or
            <codeph>3</codeph>.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_stringify">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_STRINGIFY(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns a readable summary of an HLL sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_hll_union_f">

          <dt>
            DS_HLL_UNION_F(BINARY sketch1, BINARY sketch2)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges two HLL sketches into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Ignores a <codeph>NULL</codeph> argument. Returns an
              empty sketch if both arguments are <codeph>NULL</codeph>.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_cdf_as_string">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_CDF_AS_STRING(BINARY sketch, FLOAT split_point
            [, FLOAT split_point ...])
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the fraction of the values in a KLL sketch that are
            below each split point, as a comma-separated string. The last element is the
            fraction of all the values, which is 1.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> You must specify unique split points in increasing
              order.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_n">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_N(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the number of values that a KLL sketch was created
            from.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_pmf_as_string">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_PMF_AS_STRING(BINARY sketch, FLOAT split_point
            [, FLOAT split_point ...])
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Divides the values of a KLL sketch into ranges at the split
            points and returns the fraction of the values in each range, as a
            comma-separated string. For example, the split points <codeph>1.0</codeph> and
            <codeph>3.5</codeph> create the ranges below 1.0, from 1.0 to 3.5, and from
            3.5.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> You must specify unique split points in increasing
              order.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_quantile">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_QUANTILE(BINARY sketch, DOUBLE rank)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the value at <codeph><varname>rank</varname></codeph>
            in a KLL sketch. <codeph><varname>rank</varname></codeph> is between 0 and 1.
            For example, <codeph>0.5</codeph> returns the median.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>FLOAT</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_quantiles_as_string">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_QUANTILES_AS_STRING(BINARY sketch, DOUBLE rank [, DOUBLE rank ...])
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the values at the given ranks in a KLL sketch, as a
            comma-separated string.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_rank">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_RANK(BINARY sketch, FLOAT value)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the fraction of the values in a KLL sketch that are
            less than <codeph><varname>value</varname></codeph>, as a number between 0 and
            1.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>DOUBLE</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_kll_stringify">

          <dt>
            DS_KLL_STRINGIFY(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns a readable summary of a KLL sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>STRING</codeph>
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_estimate">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_ESTIMATE(BINARY sketch)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns the distinct count estimate of a Theta sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BIGINT</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Returns 0, not <codeph>NULL</codeph>, for a
              <codeph>NULL</codeph> sketch.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_exclude">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_EXCLUDE(BINARY sketch1, BINARY sketch2)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns a Theta sketch of the values that are in
            <codeph><varname>sketch1</varname></codeph> but not in
            <codeph><varname>sketch2</varname></codeph>.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Returns <codeph>NULL</codeph> if
              <codeph><varname>sketch1</varname></codeph> is <codeph>NULL</codeph>, and
              <codeph><varname>sketch1</varname></codeph> if
              <codeph><varname>sketch2</varname></codeph> is <codeph>NULL</codeph>.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_intersect_f">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_INTERSECT_F(BINARY sketch1, BINARY sketch2)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Returns a Theta sketch of the values that are in both
            sketches.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Returns <codeph>NULL</codeph> if either argument is
              <codeph>NULL</codeph>.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

        <dlentry id="ds_theta_union_f">

          <dt>
            DS_THETA_UNION_F(BINARY sketch1, BINARY sketch2)
          </dt>

          <dd>
            <b>Purpose:</b> Merges two Theta sketches into one sketch.
            <p>
              <b>Return type:</b> <codeph>BINARY</codeph>
            </p>

            <p>
              <b>Usage notes:</b> Ignores a <codeph>NULL</codeph> argument. Returns an
              empty sketch if both arguments are <codeph>NULL</codeph>.
            </p>
          </dd>

        </dlentry>

      </dl>

    </section>

  </conbody>

</concept>
